00:33:54.500 --> 00:33:57.500
The word Advent means arrival.

00:33:58.500 --> 00:34:00.500
The season of Advent refers to two arrivals.

00:34:01.500 --> 00:34:04.500
It refers to the initial arrival of Jesus the Messiah.

00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:06.500
His birth in Bethlehem.

00:34:07.500 --> 00:34:10.500
The entrance of God in human form in the world.

00:34:11.500 --> 00:34:13.500
The second arrival is the arrival that hasn't happened yet.

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:17.500
When Jesus arrives again to make all things new.

00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:26.500
The season of Advent is this sense of anticipation and waiting and hope in these new arrivals.

00:34:27.500 --> 00:34:28.500
In the season of waiting.

00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:32.500
The season of Christmas marks the actual birth of Jesus.

00:34:32.500 --> 00:34:38.500
The season of Advent is about the anticipation of Jesus' arrival in the world simultaneously.

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:41.500
It's about the anticipation of Jesus' second arrival.

00:34:42.500 --> 00:34:48.500
The second coming to heal and renew the entire cosmos including us.

