The Bible was untouchable.

00:36:22.500 --> 00:36:31.500
It was uncriticable and as a result I felt this pressure to always be positively inclined toward Scripture.

00:36:32.500 --> 00:36:40.500
To assume that any questions I had about it was automatically my own ignorance or my stubbornness or my short-sightedness and I have plenty of those.

00:36:41.500 --> 00:36:49.500
But in my middle age also I'm allowing for the possibility that the Bible could provoke some crankiness in me.

00:36:50.500 --> 00:36:51.500
To be frustrated.

00:36:52.500 --> 00:36:53.500
With the Bible.

00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:55.500
To have questions of it.

00:36:56.500 --> 00:37:02.500
To be honest about it with God when it's just not doing it for me.

00:37:03.500 --> 00:37:04.500
And that was the case this week.

00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:08.500
I read these texts and they just weren't doing it for me.

00:37:09.500 --> 00:37:11.500
I felt all kinds of dissonance.

00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:15.500
Which might be surprising given the vision of Isaiah 2.

00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:21.500
This beautiful heart capturing picture of God's peace and justice filling the world.

00:37:22.500 --> 00:37:24.500
Everyone in union with God and with each other.

00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:31.500
Repurposing tools of war for tools of creation and cultivation and flourishing.

00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:33.500
What a beautiful vision.

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:42.500
And yet I feel dissonance when I consider that here we are some 2700 years removed from this text.

00:37:43.500 --> 00:37:50.500
And that vision feels just as far away in the future as it must have in Isaiah's day.

00:37:51.500 --> 00:37:56.500
The current administration has renamed the Department of Defense the Department of War.

00:37:57.500 --> 00:38:05.500
Speaking of war, there are so many currently underway in Ukraine and in Palestine and in several other places.

00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:11.500
We appear to be no more closer to shalom and peace today than in Isaiah's time.

00:38:12.500 --> 00:38:19.500
When Israel was complicit with injustice and violence against the least powerful and the most vulnerable.

00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:21.500
So I read the second text.

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:23.500
Psalm 122.

00:38:23.500 --> 00:38:27.500
Hoping perhaps to preach from a text that felt less dissonant.

00:38:28.500 --> 00:38:29.500
Verses 6 through 9 read.

00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:32.500
Pray for the peace of Jerusalem.

00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:34.500
May they prosper who love you.

00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:38.500
Peace be within your walls and security within your towers.

00:38:39.500 --> 00:38:43.500
For the sake of my relatives and friends I will say peace be within you.

00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:47.500
For the sake of the house of the Lord our God I will seek your good.

00:38:48.500 --> 00:38:49.500
What a beautiful prayer.

00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:59.500
And yet I read this and I couldn't help but to think of the way that peace is not in fact within Jerusalem's walls and towers today.

00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:05.500
Jerusalem has been in its latest conflict for more than a year now.

00:39:06.500 --> 00:39:10.500
Beginning more than a year ago from an assault from Hamas in October of 2024.

00:39:11.500 --> 00:39:17.500
But what causes me more dissonance is to wonder how to pray for the peace of Jerusalem.

00:39:17.500 --> 00:39:25.500
When Israel has itself become a perpetrator of great violence and death against so many Palestinians in Gaza.

00:39:26.500 --> 00:39:31.500
I want to pray for peace and for the good of Gaza who Israel would consider an enemy.

00:39:33.500 --> 00:39:34.500
More dissonance.

00:39:36.500 --> 00:39:39.500
I turn next to the New Testament text from Romans 13.

00:39:39.500 --> 00:39:48.500
In verses 11 and 12 the Apostle Paul writes salvation is nearer to us than when we became believers first.

00:39:49.500 --> 00:39:50.500
The night is far gone.

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:53.500
The day is near.

00:39:54.500 --> 00:39:56.500
Is it really Paul?

00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:58.500
The night is far gone?

00:39:59.500 --> 00:40:01.500
Did that really come true?

00:40:02.500 --> 00:40:08.500
With all that's going on in the world some 2,000 years later with the violence against undocumented immigrants.

00:40:09.500 --> 00:40:13.500
With the scapegoating and unjust treatment of our transgender siblings.

00:40:14.500 --> 00:40:17.500
With all the war and atrocity that we've already mentioned.

00:40:18.500 --> 00:40:21.500
It feels like we are in the dead of night bro.

00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:26.500
Surely Jesus has something helpful to say.

00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:29.500
The Gospel text is from Matthew 24.

00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:33.500
Where Jesus talks about what some interpret as the rapture.

00:40:34.500 --> 00:40:36.500
Two will be in the field one will be taken the other left.

00:40:36.500 --> 00:40:39.500
Two women will be grinding meal together one will be taken the other left.

00:40:40.500 --> 00:40:45.500
I am so glad that Brett solved all the problems of the rapture in the eschatology series this fall.

00:40:46.500 --> 00:40:49.500
So I can just move right past that to Jesus punchline.

00:40:50.500 --> 00:40:53.500
Where he says you don't know when the Lord is coming.

00:40:54.500 --> 00:40:55.500
So stay awake.

00:40:56.500 --> 00:40:57.500
Be alert. Be ready.

00:40:58.500 --> 00:41:01.500
The Son of Man is coming at an hour you don't expect.

00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:03.500
I don't know about you.

00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:07.500
But this text brings all my hell trauma right to the surface.

00:41:08.500 --> 00:41:10.500
Be ready or else Jesus will get you.

00:41:11.500 --> 00:41:15.500
Don't misbehave because Jesus might return right in the middle of it.

00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:18.500
I can hear that old Gospel preacher.

00:41:19.500 --> 00:41:24.500
Stoking fear to get folks to comply and obey with the church's moral norms.

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:29.500
I mean the Son of Man is even compared to a thief who comes in the middle of the night to rob someone.

00:41:30.500 --> 00:41:32.500
Stay awake so you don't get robbed.

00:41:33.500 --> 00:41:36.500
That's not a heartwarming image.

00:41:38.500 --> 00:41:39.500
More dissonance.

00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:42.500
Sorry to be such a downer y'all.

00:41:44.500 --> 00:41:50.500
Maybe, just maybe you feel some of this dissonance yourself.

00:41:51.500 --> 00:42:01.500
The dissonance between the world we currently live in and the world that is promised to arrive one day.

00:42:02.500 --> 00:42:09.500
It seems better to be honest about the dissonance than to try to spiritually bypass it.

00:42:10.500 --> 00:42:11.500
Or to sugar coat it.

00:42:12.500 --> 00:42:13.500
Or ignore it.

00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:19.500
This dissonance is exactly where I long for God to meet me.

00:42:20.500 --> 00:42:23.500
To meet us in this Advent season.

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:28.500
What would it look like for God to meet us in the midst of this dissonance?

00:42:28.500 --> 00:42:31.500
To hold this dissonance with us.

00:42:32.500 --> 00:42:36.500
To lead us through it instead of around it.

00:42:37.500 --> 00:42:40.500
That's exactly what I wondered as I sat with these texts.

00:42:41.500 --> 00:42:42.500
God, what do we do with this?

00:42:43.500 --> 00:42:48.500
What's your invitation to us in the midst of dissonance like this?

00:42:49.500 --> 00:42:56.500
What does it look like for us to faithfully anticipate your arrival in this Advent season?

00:42:57.500 --> 00:43:03.500
I'll admit that I came to these texts with some ideas about what we might do with the dissonance.

00:43:04.500 --> 00:43:05.500
Instead of avoiding it, to move through it.

00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:08.500
To let God sit with us in it.

00:43:09.500 --> 00:43:12.500
To lament the dissonance to God.

00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:17.500
To share our frustration and confusion and even anger with God.

00:43:18.500 --> 00:43:22.500
Lament after all is a very common response to dissonance in the Psalms.

00:43:23.500 --> 00:43:27.500
And certainly I commend lament as a healing practice.

00:43:28.500 --> 00:43:33.500
But as I read through the texts again and again, I began to notice something else.

00:43:34.500 --> 00:43:35.500
That addressed this dissonance.

00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:39.500
That gave me something to hold on to.

00:43:40.500 --> 00:43:44.500
Jesus mentions it in Matthew 24 when he says, keep awake.

00:43:45.500 --> 00:43:46.500
Be ready.

00:43:46.500 --> 00:43:53.500
Paul mentions it in Romans 13 when he says, let us walk decently as in the day.

00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:57.500
Put on the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:43:58.500 --> 00:44:01.500
And what do you know, there it is at the end of our Isaiah text.

00:44:02.500 --> 00:44:05.500
Oh house of Jacob, come.

00:44:06.500 --> 00:44:10.500
Let us walk in the light of the Lord.

00:44:11.500 --> 00:44:21.500
What I hear Jesus and Paul and Isaiah saying is that one way we can respond to this dissonance is with our lives.

00:44:22.500 --> 00:44:28.500
By embodying here and now in the midst of the dumpster fire of things.

00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:34.500
The future peace and goodness and justice for which we long.

00:44:35.500 --> 00:44:39.500
That's what Isaiah means when he invites Israel to walk in the light of the Lord.

00:44:40.500 --> 00:44:42.500
To walk in the ways of God.

00:44:43.500 --> 00:44:49.500
To embody in the present the peace and justice that is coming more fully in the future.

00:44:50.500 --> 00:44:54.500
When all will stream to the mountain of God and be instructed in God's ways.

00:44:55.500 --> 00:45:00.500
When humanity will repurpose its war weapons into creation tools.

00:45:00.500 --> 00:45:09.500
What if walking in the light of the Lord means that we go ahead and start living the future now?

00:45:10.500 --> 00:45:17.500
What if the most faithful form of waiting is practicing the good way of Jesus right now?

00:45:18.500 --> 00:45:22.500
To put on the Lord Jesus Christ as Paul says.

00:45:23.500 --> 00:45:27.500
The vibe of this invitation is not that it's all up to us.

00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:32.500
As if God's not going to do it and so we've got to create a different world on our own kind of thing.

00:45:33.500 --> 00:45:35.500
What if God is already doing it?

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:38.500
What if God has always been doing it?

00:45:39.500 --> 00:45:48.500
What if God's at work to heal and renew and restore and our invitation is to participate in it?

00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:54.500
Isaiah's invitation after all is to walk by the light of the Lord.

00:45:55.500 --> 00:45:56.500
We don't have to generate the light.

00:45:57.500 --> 00:45:59.500
The light doesn't begin with us.

00:46:00.500 --> 00:46:02.500
We just have to find it and walk in it.

00:46:03.500 --> 00:46:09.500
Neither is the vibe of this invitation to walk in the light of the Lord or else.

00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:14.500
Thanks be to God. Contrary to my anxieties.

00:46:15.500 --> 00:46:18.500
Or else God will get us or else God will judge us and send us to hell.

00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:24.500
It's more like the plea of someone who loves us all so dearly.

00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:28.500
Please, please walk in the light.

00:46:29.500 --> 00:46:32.500
Because the fruit of walking in the light is light.

00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:36.500
And the fruit of walking in darkness is darkness.

00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:38.500
What fruit do we want?

00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:42.500
God doesn't coerce or threaten us.

00:46:43.500 --> 00:46:46.500
The plea comes to us as an invitation to participate.

00:46:47.500 --> 00:46:49.500
To join in what the Spirit of God is doing.

00:46:49.500 --> 00:46:55.500
What the Spirit of God is doing to clothe ourselves with the character and action of Jesus.

00:46:56.500 --> 00:47:03.500
This invitation reminds me of something I've heard my co-director in the Healing Collective, Mallory Wykoff, say.

00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:10.500
That the best critique of the bad is the embodiment of the better.

00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:16.500
The best critique of the bad is the embodiment of the better.

00:47:16.500 --> 00:47:17.500
I love that.

00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:21.500
I feel like it's a place that I can put my dissonant energy.

00:47:22.500 --> 00:47:25.500
Instead of getting stuck in the dissonance, paralyzed by it.

00:47:26.500 --> 00:47:31.500
What if that was the energy that fueled me, that fueled us to embody the better?

00:47:32.500 --> 00:47:35.500
The best critique of war is the embodiment of peace.

00:47:36.500 --> 00:47:40.500
The best critique of scarcity is the embodiment of provision.

00:47:41.500 --> 00:47:45.500
The best critique of loneliness is the embodiment of belonging.

00:47:46.500 --> 00:47:51.500
The best critique of polarization is the embodiment of proximity.

00:47:52.500 --> 00:47:57.500
The best critique of apathy is the embodiment of empathy.

00:47:58.500 --> 00:48:03.500
The best critique of dehumanization is the embodiment of kindness.

00:48:04.500 --> 00:48:09.500
The best critique of injustice is the embodiment of love.

00:48:11.500 --> 00:48:17.500
A couple weeks ago, I accepted an invitation from my friend and colleague, Colin Packer,

00:48:18.500 --> 00:48:22.500
to join him and another friend of ours, David Park,

00:48:23.500 --> 00:48:30.500
at the Dallas Field Office of Immigration and Customs Enforcement, also known as ICE.

00:48:31.500 --> 00:48:38.500
Colin had been invited by a grassroots organization called Vicinos Unidos DFW,

00:48:38.500 --> 00:48:41.500
led by several Chicana women,

00:48:42.500 --> 00:48:47.500
who are showing up every day at the field office to help migrant folks know their rights

00:48:48.500 --> 00:48:53.500
and to raise awareness about the mistreatment of our undocumented neighbors by ICE.

00:48:54.500 --> 00:49:02.500
Colin and David and I were there, and we were invited specifically because we are white clergypersons.

00:49:03.500 --> 00:49:10.500
Unfortunately, and not surprisingly, ICE agents respond much differently to white male clergymembers

00:49:11.500 --> 00:49:14.500
than they do to our brown female colleagues.

00:49:15.500 --> 00:49:17.500
They yell and curse and make threats to brown women,

00:49:18.500 --> 00:49:23.500
but when a white clergyperson is present, they are respectful and calm.

00:49:24.500 --> 00:49:29.500
So our invitation was to show up and share the privilege that comes with our being white

00:49:29.500 --> 00:49:35.500
to our non-white colleagues so that they could do their work more safely, more effectively.

00:49:36.500 --> 00:49:43.500
The leaders of Vicinos Unidos asked us to find some way to identify ourselves as clergy

00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:48.500
with either a stole or a collar, and that's why I'm wearing this tonight.

00:49:49.500 --> 00:49:52.500
Both so that ICE would know that we were clergy,

00:49:52.500 --> 00:49:59.500
but also so that our neighbors would not wonder if we were casual ICE agents ourselves

00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:05.500
and become suspicious of Vicinos Unidos and their work there.

00:50:06.500 --> 00:50:11.500
And so we borrowed three stoles, one of which I'm wearing from our dear friend and colleague,

00:50:12.500 --> 00:50:14.500
Pepa Paniagua, who some of you know.

00:50:15.500 --> 00:50:19.500
She's a Presbyterian minister, and she's got stoles and spades, apparently.

00:50:20.500 --> 00:50:24.500
It's the first time I've ever worn one. This is the second time I've ever worn one.

00:50:25.500 --> 00:50:29.500
It feels a little weird, honestly, but isn't it pretty? It's so beautiful, yeah?

00:50:30.500 --> 00:50:37.500
So one Friday, a couple weeks ago, we arrived a little bit before 6 a.m. in our stoles.

00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:41.500
We met the team. We stood on the sidewalk outside the field office,

00:50:42.500 --> 00:50:47.500
ready to help however we were needed, but mostly just to stand there.

00:50:47.500 --> 00:50:52.500
Occasionally, cars would come toward us down this industrial West Dallas street,

00:50:53.500 --> 00:50:56.500
and if the cars were moving fast and sometimes blaring music,

00:50:57.500 --> 00:51:00.500
they were probably ICE agents checking in for their shift.

00:51:01.500 --> 00:51:06.500
I noticed in big letters on the back of one truck entering the employee parking lot,

00:51:07.500 --> 00:51:08.500
Jesus saves.

00:51:09.500 --> 00:51:14.500
I could feel the tension and anger in my body as those cars raced by,

00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:17.500
many without license plates, so that they couldn't be identified.

00:51:18.500 --> 00:51:22.500
I noticed as I looked over that my friend and colleague David

00:51:23.500 --> 00:51:29.500
was waving at the ICE agents as they came in, and that humanized them for me.

00:51:30.500 --> 00:51:35.500
I was like, oh, I needed that. I felt the difference, the opposition there,

00:51:36.500 --> 00:51:39.500
and some would see the stoles, and they would wave back at us.

00:51:39.500 --> 00:51:42.500
Oh, something felt shifted.

00:51:46.500 --> 00:51:48.500
We wondered if they were worried about their own families.

00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:52.500
We wondered if their families were worried about them.

00:51:53.500 --> 00:51:56.500
If the cars were moving slowly down the street,

00:51:57.500 --> 00:52:02.500
they were usually our neighbors showing up for their immigration check-in appointments.

00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:06.500
Our colleagues would wave down the slow-moving cars and invite them to talk,

00:52:06.500 --> 00:52:09.500
and if they were willing, they would pull into an adjacent parking lot

00:52:10.500 --> 00:52:15.500
where our colleagues would let them know that ICE was detaining high numbers of people

00:52:16.500 --> 00:52:19.500
showing up for their routine immigration check-ins.

00:52:20.500 --> 00:52:24.500
They encouraged them to sign a form that would allow Vicinos Unidos

00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:29.500
to contact their family, to be able to track them in the system.

00:52:30.500 --> 00:52:33.500
Otherwise, there'd be no way to know where they went, where they were,

00:52:33.500 --> 00:52:35.500
what their status was.

00:52:36.500 --> 00:52:39.500
Detainees are sometimes transferred out of state on purpose

00:52:40.500 --> 00:52:44.500
to make it difficult to impede their deportation process.

00:52:45.500 --> 00:52:49.500
Our colleagues also encouraged them to park in the adjacent lot

00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:55.500
and not in the ICE parking lot because ICE has contracts with local towing companies

00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:59.500
to impound cars that stay in their lot.

00:52:59.500 --> 00:53:03.500
If they came with family members, our colleagues encouraged their family members to leave

00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:06.500
because ICE agents would often ask,

00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:09.500
do you have family waiting for you?

00:53:10.500 --> 00:53:13.500
And if they do, it's not uncommon for ICE to go out in the parking lot

00:53:14.500 --> 00:53:17.500
and detain the family members as well.

00:53:18.500 --> 00:53:21.500
Occasionally, we were asked to pray for our neighbors

00:53:22.500 --> 00:53:25.500
who were walking to the field office for their appointments,

00:53:25.500 --> 00:53:29.500
and we prayed for peace and protection as they trembled.

00:53:31.500 --> 00:53:36.500
Sometimes clergy members were asked to escort our colleagues and neighbors

00:53:37.500 --> 00:53:40.500
to the door of the field office to inquire about their family members

00:53:41.500 --> 00:53:45.500
who had been inside for longer than expected and might be detained.

00:53:46.500 --> 00:53:49.500
I watched as one pregnant woman came back with her small child

00:53:50.500 --> 00:53:53.500
and returned from asking about her husband.

00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:56.500
She wept as she learned that he had been detained.

00:53:57.500 --> 00:54:01.500
Our colleagues gave her a place to sit and food to eat.

00:54:02.500 --> 00:54:06.500
They played with her son as she processed the news that she had just received.

00:54:07.500 --> 00:54:13.500
I listened as David asked Noemi, one of the founders of Vicinos Unidos DFW,

00:54:14.500 --> 00:54:16.500
how she came into this work.

00:54:17.500 --> 00:54:20.500
And with tears in her eyes, she shared how her own father

00:54:20.500 --> 00:54:23.500
had been deported when she was young.

00:54:24.500 --> 00:54:27.500
She knows what it's like, and she wants to help other people

00:54:28.500 --> 00:54:30.500
who are in similar circumstances.

00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:35.500
And so she gets up every day early to come to the field office

00:54:36.500 --> 00:54:40.500
to help her neighbors before she goes in to her full-time job.

00:54:42.500 --> 00:54:46.500
Noemi might not use this language, but she and her colleagues

00:54:47.500 --> 00:54:51.500
are walking in the light of the Lord.

00:54:52.500 --> 00:54:56.500
In the midst of the dissonance of detention and mass deportation

00:54:57.500 --> 00:54:59.500
and mistreatment of undocumented neighbors,

00:55:00.500 --> 00:55:03.500
in the midst of injustice, they accepted the invitation

00:55:04.500 --> 00:55:08.500
to participate in God's peace and justice and goodness.

00:55:09.500 --> 00:55:12.500
To critique the bad by embodying the better.

00:55:12.500 --> 00:55:17.500
To anticipate with their active bodies the renewed and healed world

00:55:18.500 --> 00:55:19.500
that is to come.

00:55:20.500 --> 00:55:23.500
The world we hope for in the second coming of the Christ

00:55:24.500 --> 00:55:26.500
in this Advent season.

00:55:27.500 --> 00:55:31.500
I wonder, how might the Spirit be inviting you

00:55:32.500 --> 00:55:35.500
to walk in the light of the Lord this Advent?

00:55:36.500 --> 00:55:39.500
To embody the goodness of God.

00:55:40.500 --> 00:55:45.500
Where do you long for more peace and goodness and justice

00:55:46.500 --> 00:55:48.500
and belonging around you?

00:55:49.500 --> 00:55:53.500
What opportunities to embody those longings

00:55:54.500 --> 00:55:57.500
is the Spirit sending your way?

00:55:58.500 --> 00:56:01.500
We don't have to fabricate the opportunities.

00:56:02.500 --> 00:56:05.500
We simply have to pay attention for what the Spirit

00:56:05.500 --> 00:56:10.500
might be sending toward us and cooperate with it.

00:56:11.500 --> 00:56:13.500
Go with the flow of it.

00:56:14.500 --> 00:56:16.500
And if it seems daunting, I hear you.

00:56:17.500 --> 00:56:20.500
There's some risk in accepting such an invitation.

00:56:21.500 --> 00:56:25.500
I am usually pretty anxious to accept the invitation myself.

00:56:26.500 --> 00:56:28.500
So it's normal. You're in good company.

00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:31.500
And I hope you'll be kind to yourself

00:56:32.500 --> 00:56:34.500
in the midst of the dauntingness of it.

00:56:35.500 --> 00:56:40.500
The good news is that the invitation is to us collectively.

00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:44.500
Let us walk in the light of the Lord.

00:56:45.500 --> 00:56:49.500
This embodiment work is something we get to do together.

00:56:50.500 --> 00:56:54.500
Something I got to do with my brothers, Colin and David.

00:56:55.500 --> 00:56:59.500
If we long for peace in our world, let us be a community of peace.

00:57:00.500 --> 00:57:02.500
If we long for belonging in our world,

00:57:02.500 --> 00:57:05.500
let us be a community of belonging.

00:57:06.500 --> 00:57:10.500
If we long for the recognition of the image of God in all of humanity,

00:57:11.500 --> 00:57:16.500
let us be a community that recognizes the image of God in each other.

00:57:17.500 --> 00:57:19.500
If we long for generosity in our world,

00:57:20.500 --> 00:57:22.500
let us be a community of generosity.

00:57:23.500 --> 00:57:24.500
If we long for justice in our world,

00:57:25.500 --> 00:57:27.500
let us be a community of justice.

00:57:28.500 --> 00:57:33.500
Come, let us walk in the light of the Lord.

00:57:34.500 --> 00:57:39.500
In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and the Holy Spirit. Amen.

00:57:45.500 --> 00:57:47.500
It is time for communion.

00:57:49.500 --> 00:57:52.500
At the table we practice open communion.

00:57:53.500 --> 00:57:56.500
So all are welcome to participate who wish to.

00:57:57.500 --> 00:58:02.500
We go row by row from the front to the back to this center aisle all the way up

00:58:03.500 --> 00:58:05.500
to receive the bread and the cup.

00:58:06.500 --> 00:58:10.500
As you take the cup, just know that the red is wine and the white is juice.

00:58:11.500 --> 00:58:15.500
And you are welcome to spend some time in prayer or kneeling up here at the front

00:58:16.500 --> 00:58:20.500
or to return to your seat, whatever is most comfortable and preferable to you.

00:58:21.500 --> 00:58:26.500
This is the table, not of the church, but of the Lord.

00:58:27.500 --> 00:58:32.500
It's made ready for those who love Him and for those who want to love Him more.

00:58:33.500 --> 00:58:38.500
So come, you who have much faith and you who have little.

00:58:39.500 --> 00:58:43.500
You who have been here often and you who have not been here long.

00:58:44.500 --> 00:58:47.500
You who have tried to follow and you who have failed.

00:58:47.500 --> 00:58:51.500
Come, because it is the Lord who invites you.

00:58:52.500 --> 00:58:56.500
It's His will that those who want Him should meet Him here.

00:58:57.500 --> 00:58:59.500
Come to the table.

00:59:17.500 --> 00:59:19.500
Come to the table.

00:59:47.500 --> 00:59:49.500
Come to the table.

01:00:17.500 --> 01:00:20.500
Come.

01:00:47.500 --> 01:00:48.500
Come.

01:00:48.500 --> 01:00:49.500
Come.

01:00:49.500 --> 01:00:50.500
Come.

01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:50.500


01:01:47.500 --> 01:01:54.500
Come.

01:01:54.500 --> 01:02:02.500
Come.

01:02:02.500 --> 01:02:02.500


01:02:06.820 --> 01:02:10.379
Tonight we're going to end with a prayer.

01:02:10.379 --> 01:02:25.820
I know it might be new for some of you as we've only done it once or twice here, but

01:02:25.820 --> 01:02:32.340
if you guys would stand with us in this prayer and just receive this as you go into your

01:02:32.340 --> 01:02:39.340
week and let it lead us into that freedom, that hope for what is to come, that embodiment

01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:43.340
of walking in the light of Christ.

01:02:50.340 --> 01:03:06.340
Would you take, Lord, and receive my liberty, my memory, my understanding, and my will,

01:03:06.340 --> 01:03:13.340
all that I call my own?

01:03:13.340 --> 01:03:35.340
Give me only your loving grace, your loving grace.

01:03:35.340 --> 01:03:41.340
That is enough.

01:03:41.340 --> 01:03:55.340
That is enough for me.

01:03:55.340 --> 01:04:07.340
You have given all to me.

01:04:07.340 --> 01:04:13.340
To you, Lord, I return it.

01:04:13.340 --> 01:04:18.340
Everything belongs to you.

01:04:18.340 --> 01:04:25.340
Do with it what you will.

01:04:25.340 --> 01:04:47.340
Give me only your loving grace, your loving grace.

01:04:47.340 --> 01:04:53.340
That is enough.

01:04:53.340 --> 01:05:06.340
That is enough for me.

01:05:06.340 --> 01:05:14.340
For me.

01:05:17.340 --> 01:05:34.340
Thank you so much for joining us this evening.

01:05:34.340 --> 01:05:39.340
Thank you, Charles, for that wonderful message.

01:05:39.340 --> 01:05:47.340
If you are new, we would love for you to fill out a card at the table or an online

01:05:47.340 --> 01:05:52.340
visitor card by scanning the QR code.

01:05:52.340 --> 01:05:56.340
Just to let you know, we could reach out and let you know that we're glad that you joined

01:05:56.340 --> 01:05:58.340
us.

01:05:58.340 --> 01:06:02.340
Generosity is a key aspect of life, of adoration and worship.

01:06:03.340 --> 01:06:12.340
To give financially, you can scan the QR code or visit the table at thetabletx.org.

01:06:12.340 --> 01:06:21.340
If you call the table home but don't currently have a meetup, you may go into the table,

01:06:21.340 --> 01:06:27.340
tx.org, and there are several meetups that you can choose from and find one that fits

01:06:27.340 --> 01:06:37.340
your schedule and your time and have a meetup with the different folks in the community.

01:06:37.340 --> 01:06:43.340
Also, if you are not part of a ministry team and you are interested in that, we have several

01:06:43.340 --> 01:06:49.340
ministries that, if that's something that sounds like you would like to do, there's

01:06:49.340 --> 01:06:55.340
the host team and the AV team and also our praise team and our kids ministry.

01:06:55.340 --> 01:07:01.340
So, you can find something that works for you.

01:07:01.340 --> 01:07:04.340
Alright, let me send you out with this benediction.

01:07:04.340 --> 01:07:11.340
You may hold your hand down in a posture to receive or just open your hearts to these

01:07:11.340 --> 01:07:14.340
words.

01:07:14.340 --> 01:07:20.340
You are a child of God.

01:07:20.340 --> 01:07:25.340
You are a child of God.

01:07:25.340 --> 01:07:32.340
This is true on your best day and this is true on your worst day.

01:07:32.340 --> 01:07:38.340
So, as you go into your week ahead with its yet to be determined highs and lows and everything

01:07:38.340 --> 01:07:48.340
in between, go filled with the assurance that you are loved, that you are worthy, and that

01:07:49.340 --> 01:07:53.340
you are accepted just as you are.

01:07:53.340 --> 01:07:59.340
And go filled with God's Holy Spirit and the desire to extend these same gifts of grace

01:07:59.340 --> 01:08:04.340
and unconditional love to everyone you come in contact with.

01:08:04.340 --> 01:08:06.340
Be blessed.

01:08:06.340 --> 01:08:11.340
Have a great week and we'll see you again next Sunday.

01:08:18.339 --> 01:08:34.339
Give me only your love and grace.

01:08:34.339 --> 01:08:40.339
That is enough.

01:08:40.339 --> 01:08:46.339
That is enough.

01:08:46.339 --> 01:08:52.339
For me.

01:08:52.339 --> 01:09:00.339
For me.

